course: dictionary
lesson: 3787
title: Footman: a servant in a grand house
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A footman is a servant who works in a big, grand house. Read the clues around the word to work out what he does. «A footman with a face like a fish hands a giant letter to a footman with a face like a frog.» Footmen carry letters and messages, so they are the people who deliver things for the family.
explain: Footmen also open doors and serve food at the table. In Alice, the Frog-Footman is the servant who should open doors, so a footman's job is about helping the people who live in the house. When you meet a new word, ask: what does this person do? The clues will tell you.
explain: Alice's footmen are silly. «I shall sit here till tomorrow—or next day, maybe.» A real footman would not sit outside a door for days. The author makes the Frog-Footman ridiculous to show how silly rules and manners can be.
fact: A footman is a male servant in a grand house.
fact: A footman wears a uniform, opens doors, serves food at table and carries messages.
fact: Footmen worked in large houses and palaces in the past, and they still work at Buckingham Palace today.
fact: In Alice in Wonderland, the Fish-Footman brings the Duchess an invitation to play croquet, and the Frog-Footman takes it.
fact: Both Alice footmen wear powdered wigs, which were a fashion in the past.
exercise: What is a footman? | A soldier who fights on foot | A powdered wig worn by a queen | *A male servant in a grand house who wears a uniform | A person who walks very far every day
exercise: Which jobs does a footman do? | Sails ships across the sea | *Opens doors and serves food at the table | Cuts the grass and grows the flowers | Makes the beds in the palace kitchen
exercise: The Frog-Footman says he will sit there «till tomorrow». What does this tell you? | He works all night as a guard | He is really a frog who lives in the house | He is so tired that he must sleep | *He is being silly, and the author is making fun of him
test: In Alice in Wonderland, which footman brings the Duchess an invitation from the Queen? | *The Fish-Footman | The Cheshire Cat | The Mad Hatter | The White Rabbit
test: Footmen still work today at which famous palace? | Windsor Forest | Hogwarts Castle | *Buckingham Palace | The Tower of Pisa
exam: What does the word footman mean? | A soldier who fights on foot | A person who walks very far | A powdered wig worn at parties | *A male servant in a grand house who wears a uniform and opens doors
